      "writtenOn": "2023-01-23T23:12:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason this is like it is is because if you start a merge, and then you want to restart it again, then we would like to be able to continue from this point, rather than syncing again. So, this flag is supposed to represent whether you want all new code OR to use the existing code.\n\nWe could split this into two flags (separate Android and upstream crosvm sync), but I do thing the \"touch nothing at all\" option is important. WDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "3257c1f9497cbfe65c01a1d680e8165d980a784b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "45554246_e7ec982b",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1644679
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-23T23:32:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you have a concrete use case for \"touch nothing at all\" in merge-setup.sh? I\u0027m having a hard time thinking of a case that I would want to do that.\n\n`merge-setup.sh -s`\n\u003csomething bad happens\u003e\n`repo abandon merge`\n`merge-setup.sh` # to get to the same point previously and avoid any new upstream CLs from Android OR crosvm?\n\nWhy wouldn\u0027t we want new upstream commits from crosvm?",
      "parentUuid": "e9514843_908f5584",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "3257c1f9497cbfe65c01a1d680e8165d980a784b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b08d599_66faf29e",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-23T23:42:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s the exact usecase - to get to the same point we got to previously, if you need to restart a merge. I\u0027ve had to do this a few times, because I was rabbit-holing on an issue or because I learned of an easier way to do things. I also know Elie ran into this at one point because his CL got squashed or something like this, we might ask him, but I recall the way he found the exact point again was because of FETCH_HEAD there.\n\nOf course - if we got to a point somewhere, we should be able to restore our old CL. However, we can\u0027t always rely on having a working CL uploaded/backed up, so being able to restore to the same point, without introducing potential new issues from a sync is useful.\n\nIf you feel strongly about it, it\u0027s fine.",
      "parentUuid": "45554246_e7ec982b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "3257c1f9497cbfe65c01a1d680e8165d980a784b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cb5ff5c5_e3a4866a",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1644679
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T00:00:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand restarting the merge, but I don\u0027t know why it needs to be at the same commit of upstream crosvm. We aren\u0027t choosing specific commits when we start the merge, so it seems like it would be fine to take new commits when we restart.\n\nBut, I don\u0027t feel strongly about it. I can just sync every time I want to start a merge. It\u0027s probably better that way anyways.",
      "parentUuid": "9b08d599_66faf29e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 10,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "3257c1f9497cbfe65c01a1d680e8165d980a784b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01759f28_534651ee",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 10,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T01:17:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason is, imagine you are running into issue A, and in restarting the merge, you resync the codebase, and now you have to deal with issue A and issue B (recently introduced). So, we were experiencing a problem we weren\u0027t able to resolve the first try, and then now we have an even larger problem.\n\nWe could also be saying the opposite: we want to update crosvm all the time, so we might as well sync more. However, we already have a process for that.\n\nAnd yeah - it doesn\u0027t matter that much, but we did hit the issue B case before, and this would have saved some time. It may be the case we\u0027ll never hit it again, especially if we can increase the frequency and decrease the number of manual steps in this process.",
      "parentUuid": "cb5ff5c5_e3a4866a",
